        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you strip paint off a deck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, but expect roughly three times the labour of stripping stain. Paint forms a continuous film on top of the wood rather than penetrating it, so it needs a stronger stripper, a much longer dwell, and hands-on scraping of every square foot. Two applications are normal on a deck with several coats."
          }
