            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A caustic, sodium hydroxide based product in a thickened or gel form. The gel matters as much as the chemistry, because paint needs 20 to 45 minutes of dwell and a thin liquid dries long before then. Soy or DBE-based removers are gentler and work over hours, which suits small decks and heavy landscaping below."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I strip or sand paint off my deck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Often both. Sanding is faster on flat, accessible boards and creates no runoff; chemical stripping is the only practical route for railings, spindles and moulded profiles. Many deck jobs are best done as a hybrid. You must strip fully, not sand partially, if you intend to go back to a penetrating stain."
          }
