            "text": "For paint, typically 20 to 45 minutes, but watch it rather than time it: you want the film to wrinkle, lift or go visibly gummy. Never let it dry, and never over-dwell either, because a caustic stripper left too long on softwood raises grain badly and darkens the wood further."
