          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need to neutralise after stripping a deck?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "After a caustic stripper, yes, always. It leaves the wood strongly alkaline and darkened, and alkaline wood takes stain unevenly and can react with it. An oxalic or citric acid brightener neutralises the surface and restores the colour. It is part of the process rather than an optional finishing touch."
          }
